/E (process of evaluating handwritten answer scripts with improved accuracy, efficiency, and consistency. Traditional manual evaluation methods are often time-consuming, prone to human error, and may lack uniformity in grading. To address these challenges, the proposed system integrates Artificial Intelligence techniques such as image processing, Optical Character Recognition \(OCR\), and Natural Language Processing \(NLP\) to analyze and assess handwritten responses effectively. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
506 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 222 0 R
/E (The system first captures handwritten documents in digital form and preprocesses them to enhance image quality, remove noise, and segment text regions. OCR techniques are then applied to convert handwritten content into machine-readable text. Following this, NLP algorithms are used to interpret the extracted text, understand its semantic meaning, and compare it with predefined model answers or evaluation rubrics. The system assigns scores based on accuracy, relevance, and completeness of the response, ensuring objective and unbiased evaluation. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
507 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 222 0 R
/E (Additionally, the system is capable of handling diverse handwriting styles and provides meaningful feedback to students, highlighting areas of improvement. It significantly reduces the workload of educators, minimizes evaluation time, and enhances scalability for large volumes of answer scripts. This makes it highly suitable for academic institutions, online examinations, and large-scale competitive assessments. Overall, the AI Handwritten Evaluation System contributes to a more reliable, transparent, and efficient examination process by leveraging modern AI-driven methodologies. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
