/P 231 0 R
/T (Recent studies have focused on integrating OCR and NLP into a unified framework to create intelligent systems capable of evaluating handwritten responses. This integration allows the system to first convert handwritten text into digital form and then analyze the content for grading. Such systems aim to replicate human evaluation by considering both the correctness and quality of answers. )
/E (Recent studies have focused on integrating OCR and NLP into a unified framework to create intelligent systems capable of evaluating handwritten responses. This integration allows the system to first convert handwritten text into digital form and then analyze the content for grading. Such systems aim to replicate human evaluation by considering both the correctness and quality of answers. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
634 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 231 0 R
/T (Despite these advancements, several challenges remain in the field. Variability in handwriting styles, poor image quality, and incomplete or ambiguous answers can affect recognition and evaluation accuracy. Additionally, ensuring fairness and avoiding bias in automated grading systems is a critical concern. Researchers are exploring techniques such as explainable AI \(XAI\) to make evaluation decisions more transparent and trustworthy. )
/E (Despite these advancements, several challenges remain in the field. Variability in handwriting styles, poor image quality, and incomplete or ambiguous answers can affect recognition and evaluation accuracy. Additionally, ensuring fairness and avoiding bias in automated grading systems is a critical concern. Researchers are exploring techniques such as explainable AI \(XAI\) to make evaluation decisions more transparent and trustworthy. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
