717 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 235 0 R
/T (4.5 Handling Handwritten Text Variability )
/E (4.5 Handling Handwritten Text Variability )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
718 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 235 0 R
/E (Handling variations in handwritten text is one ofthemostchallenging aspects of designing an AI-based handwritten evaluation system. Unlike printed text, handwriting differs significantly from person to person in terms of style, size, spacing, alignment, and stroke patterns. These variations can affect the accuracy of text recognition and, consequently, the evaluation process. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
719 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 235 0 R
/E (To address these challenges, the system employs advanced deep learning models trained on diverse handwriting datasets. By exposing the model to a wide range of handwriting styles during training, it learns to generalize better and accurately recognize different writing patterns. This improves the robustness and adaptability of the system in real-world scenarios. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
720 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 235 0 R
/E (Preprocessing techniques play a crucial role in reducing variability. Steps such as noise removal, skew correction, contrast enhancement, and normalization help standardize input images before they are processed by the OCR model. These techniques ensure that variations caused by scanning errors, lighting conditions, or paper quality are minimized. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
721 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 235 0 R
/E (Additionally, data augmentation techniques are used to further enhance model performance. Methods such as rotation, scaling, flipping, and distortion are applied to training images to simulate different handwriting conditions. This helps the model become more resilient to variations and improves its ability to handle unseen handwriting styles. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
