>>
endobj
738 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E (Theperformance of the system is evaluated using metrics such as accuracy, precision, recall, and consistency with human grading. Overall, this module ensures efficient, reliable, and transparent evaluation of handwritten answers while supporting student learning through constructive feedback. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
739 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
740 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E (The system compares the extracted answer with predefined model answers or marking schemes using semantic similarity techniques rather than simple keyword matching. This allows the system to evaluate answers based on relevance, correctness, and completeness, even if the wording differs. Important features such as key concepts, sentence structure, and logical flow are considered during scoring. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
741 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E (A scoring mechanism is implemented to assign marks based on predefined criteria. The system ensures consistency and fairness in evaluation by applying the same standards to all responses, eliminating human bias. In addition, partial marking can be provided for answers that are partially correct, improving evaluation accuracy. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
742 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E (Thefeedback generation component provides detailed insights to students, highlighting correct points, missing concepts, and areas for improvement. This helps students understand their mistakes andenhances their learning experience. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
