1003 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 252 0 R
/E (TheAIHandwritten Evaluation System developed in thisproject demonstratesanefficient approach for automating the evaluation of handwritten answers. By integrating image preprocessing techniques with Tesseract OCR, the system successfully converts handwritten text into a machine-readable format. The extracted text is then evaluated using a similarity-based approach, enabling automatic calculation of marks, grades, and feedback. )
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1004 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 252 0 R
/E (The system reduces manual effort, minimizes human bias, and ensures faster evaluation compared to traditional methods. The implementation using Python, OpenCV, and OCR techniques provides a practical and cost-effective solution for academic assessment. Additionally, the ability to generate PDF reports enhances usability and makes the system suitable for real-world applications such as schools and online examinations. )
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1005 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 252 0 R
/E (Overall, the project highlights the potential of combining OCR and simple natural language processing techniques to build intelligent evaluation systems. )
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
