2806 0 obj
<<
/Title (In addition to text recognition, Natural Language Processing \(NLP\) plays a crucial role in understanding and evaluating the content of student answers. Earlier systems relied on keyword matching techniques, which often failed to capture the actual meaning and context of responses. Modern NLP techniques, including semantic analysis and transformer-based models, enable systems to evaluate answers based on relevance, coherence, and completeness, leading to more accurate grading.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2804 0 R
/Next 2808 0 R
>>
endobj
2807 0 obj
<<
/Title (Department of CSE \(AI & ML\), SOE, DSU)
/Dest [42 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2809 0 R
/Next 2805 0 R
>>
endobj
2808 0 obj
<<
/Title (Several research studies have explored automated essay scoring systems, which evaluate typed responses using machine learning algorithms. While these systems demonstrate good performance, they are limited to digital text inputs and do not address the challenges of handwritten answer evaluation. This gap has led to the development of AI-based systems that combine OCR and NLP to create a complete evaluation pipeline for handwritten responses.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2806 0 R
/Next 2810 0 R
>>
endobj
2809 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [42 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2811 0 R
/Next 2807 0 R
>>
endobj
2810 0 obj
<<
/Title (Despite significant progress, challenges still exist in this domain. Variations in handwriting styles, ambiguity in language, and differences in answer structure can affect evaluation accuracy. Additionally, ensuring fairness and avoiding bias in automated grading systems remains an important concern. Researchers are continuously working on improving model accuracy, interpretability, and robustness to overcome these limitations.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2808 0 R
/Next 2812 0 R
>>
endobj
2811 0 obj
<<
